Subject: workspace package: Claxedo's dependencies, subpaths and test runner

What: the kit is a workspace package of this monorepo, not a published npm package.
- depends on @claxedo/helpers (theme and transcript parsers use its guards) and
  exposes ./utils/* for the app's one door (src/ui/index.ts);
- dependencies are only what src/ imports; upstream lists 13 it never imports
  (luxon, dompurify, morphdom, strip-ansi, remend, diff, @shikijs/*, ...);
- `test` writes the JUnit report CI publishes (.artifacts/unit/junit.xml) under the
  repo's test deadline wrapper;
- tsconfig resolves workspace packages through their `development` export, so a
  typecheck reads sibling source and never needs a build;
- script/pack.ts and script/publish.ts are removed: they import @opencode-ai/script,
  which this repository does not have, and the kit is never published from here;
- the ./storybook/* subpaths and the story and MDX exclusions in `files` and both
  tsconfigs are removed: sync-upstream vendors no stories and nothing runs Storybook.
Why: without these the kit does not typecheck or test inside this workspace.

